Create a query optimization guide:
cat > /tmp/query_optimization_tips.md << 'EOF'
# Wazuh Query Optimization Tips

## 1. Use Filters Instead of Queries
- Use `filter` context for exact matches
- Use `query` context only for relevance scoring

## 2. Limit Result Size
- Use `size: 0` for aggregation-only queries
- Specify appropriate `size` values for result queries

## 3. Use Appropriate Field Types
- Use `.keyword` fields for exact matches
- Use analyzed fields for full-text search

## 4. Optimize Time Ranges
- Use specific time ranges instead of open-ended queries
- Consider using `now-1h` instead of `now-1d` when possible

## 5. Efficient Aggregations
- Use `min_doc_count` to filter out low-frequency results
- Limit aggregation size with appropriate `size` parameter

## 6. Index Patterns
- Use specific index patterns instead of wildcards when possible
- Consider time-based index patterns for better performance
EOF
